do_1 = "Extract the instrument definitions at interchain/modules/apps/transfer/keeper/metrics.go:11 into a transferMetrics type and newTransferMetrics constructor accepting a metric.Meter; use the same constructor for package initialization, preserving the scope, names, descriptions, types and units at metrics.go:9 through :36 and the actual callback instrument handles used by relay.go:207, :216, :306 and :315."
do_2 = "Add a test-only BindTransferMetricsForTest helper in interchain/modules/apps/transfer/keeper/export_test.go that saves the keeper meter and instrument handles, recreates them directly from the supplied provider through newTransferMetrics, and returns a restoration closure; replace the global provider installation at interchain/modules/apps/transfer/keeper/repair_m1205_test.go:155 with this binding and restore the saved handles before provider shutdown, without changing the global OpenTelemetry provider."
do_3 = "Add TestTransferMetricsProviderRestoration beside the test-only helper using real SDK providers to assert the saved keeper meter and all four instrument handles are restored and the global provider is unchanged; repeat TestRepairM_1205_MetricContract twice in one binary, retaining the real MsgTransfer and relay path at interchain/modules/apps/transfer/keeper/repair_m1205_test.go:163 through :172 and every legacy and OpenTelemetry name, type, unit, label, amount and branch assertion through :270."
